WEBVTT

00:05:56.615 --> 00:06:00.180
and otherwise might not be able
to be included in my music.

00:06:01.679 --> 00:06:04.248
And it really wasn't
until this collaboration

00:06:04.272 --> 00:06:07.002
that I had thought of the fact
that though I work so much

00:06:07.026 --> 00:06:08.753
in diversity and inclusion,

00:06:08.777 --> 00:06:11.963
that my music may not be reaching
as many people as it could be.

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:16.394
I grew up in New York City,
playing the drums,

00:06:16.418 --> 00:06:19.450
listening to Nas, Lauryn Hill,
Thievery Corporation,

00:06:19.474 --> 00:06:20.709
TV on the Radio,

00:06:20.733 --> 00:06:21.883
the Spice Girls --

00:06:23.099 --> 00:06:24.925
And for me, music was truth.

00:06:24.949 --> 00:06:28.635
Music was my perspective
into somebody else's point of view,

00:06:28.659 --> 00:06:29.810
into storytelling,

00:06:29.834 --> 00:06:31.927
into understanding how the world works.